  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 240 AM EDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\n- Sunny today, increasing clouds Friday\n\nSkies are clear across the region due to high pressure at the\nsurface and aloft moving over the Great Lakes. We'll see sunny\nskies today and highs in the mid to upper 80s. Today will feel a\nlittle humid as dewpoints climb into the lower 60s.\n\nAs the ridge moves east Friday, the next system upstream will\nspread clouds eastward and skies will become cloudy Friday\nafternoon.\n\n- Showers and isolated storms Friday night & Saturday\n\nLow pressure over the plains accompanied by an upper short wave\nwill push showers and thunderstorms eastward across the lower\nGreat Lakes Friday night. Models track the low south of the cwa,\nwhich means highest moisture content will also remain south, along\nwith the severe weather threat which will reside over the Missouri\nValley. QPF in the quarter to third of an inch range is expected\nwith lowest amounts over the northern cwa. Showers will develop\nearly Friday evening and end Saturday afternoon as the surface low\nand upper trough move east.  \n\n- Dry late weekend through mid week\n\nHigh pressure will quickly build in behind the departing low\nproducing dry weather Sunday through late Tuesday. Highs in the\nlower to mid 80s are expected during this period, which are near\nto slightly above normal.",
